# Detection: Port Scan
# MITRE ATT&CK: T1046 (Network Service Discovery)
# Telemetry: Windows Filtering Platform (Security 5156 allowed / 5157 blocked)
#
# Why WFP and not Sysmon EID 3: Sysmon network events are process-attributed,
# so they are blind to scan hits on CLOSED ports (no process, no event). WFP
# connection logging records every attempt, open or closed, so it actually
# sees the full sweep.
#
# Enable WFP auditing first (admin, on the Windows host):
#   auditpol /set /subcategory:"Filtering Platform Connection" /success:enable /failure:enable
#   (turn it back off after testing; it is chatty)
#
# Alert: scheduled every 5 min, Last 5 min window, results > 0,
#        throttle 30 min by Source_Address. Severity: Medium.

index=win-security sourcetype="WinEventLog:Security" (EventCode=5156 OR EventCode=5157)
| stats dc(Dest_Port) AS ports by Source_Address
| where ports > 20
